# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EZwallet – environment variables (server-side)
#
# Local dev : copy this file to `.env.txt` and fill in the real values.
#             (`dev-server.js` reads `.env.txt`; that file is already in .gitignore)
# Production: khai trong Cloudflare Pages → Settings → Environment variables.
#
# ⚠️ NEVER commit a real key to git.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Circle Programmable Wallets (User-Controlled) – API key server-side.
# Get it at: https://console.circle.com  →  API Keys
# The code accepts either name: API_KEY (preferred) or CIRCLE_API_KEY.
API_KEY=

# Circle Stablecoin Kit – the key for the swap flow (routed through LiFi).
# Only needed if you want the Swap feature.
KIT_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT secrets – for reference:
#
# VITE_MOCK=1   → turn on MOCK MODE (fake wallet + fake balances, Circle bypassed).
#                 Already set in `.env.mock`, run it with: npm run mock
#
# The public IDs live directly in the source (not secrets, safe to expose):
#   - Circle APP_ID        : src/screens/Login.jsx, src/screens/EnterEmail.jsx
#   - Google OAuth CLIENT_ID: src/circle.js
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
